1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,870
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,640
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,210
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,850
(Episode 53)

5
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,750
Eun Seol.

6
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:18,490
Ko Eun Seol.

7
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:22,490
Mom...

8
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:34,140
That's right, Eun Seol.

9
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:47,450
It's me, your mom.

10
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:55,760
Looks like your fever has broken.

11
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:00,800
Thank you.

12
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,400
Director.

13
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:06,910
It's okay.

14
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:09,610
Let's take things slow.

15
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,010
I'll be by your side
for the rest of my life,

16
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,580
so there's no need to rush.

17
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:19,220
When your mind is heavy,

18
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,750
your body gets exhausted, too.

19
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:24,490
Of course you're confused.

20
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,990
It's only natural
that you find it hard to believe.

21
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,740
I...

22
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:42,570
have a question, Ms. Joo.

23
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,110
Has my biological father...

24
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:52,050
ever reached out even once
since then?

25
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:55,720
No.

26
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:59,220
I desperately ran away...

27
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:02,160
so that he wouldn't find me.

28
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:27,790
Even after 30 years,

29
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:30,520
the scars haven't faded.

30
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:35,690
Still,

31
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:37,860
finding you, even late,

32
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,830
and being together like this...

33
00:02:40,130 --> 00:02:42,370
makes up for all that lost time.

34
00:02:47,970 --> 00:02:48,970
Eun Seol,

35
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:52,410
let's take our time
getting to know each other.

36
00:02:58,680 --> 00:02:59,750
Would you like some water?

37
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:06,990
Here, drink.

38
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:12,530
So, 160 dollars
from handing out flyers.

39
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,670
Right.

40
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:17,000
And from running errands...

41
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,400
That's 30 dollars.

42
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,510
That's all we made today.

43
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:24,080
How is it possible
to save 5,000 dollars at this rate?

44
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,340
Then how about this?

45
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:28,910
We'll just say we lost 5,000 dollars
somewhere...

46
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:31,180
while hunting for a place.

47
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,490
Would you believe that
if you were her?

48
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,560
Fine. There really is only one way.

49
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,160
We have to go and tell the truth.

50
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:45,330
I'll see you when you get back.

51
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,400
Where are you going?

52
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,670
You have to come with me.

53
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,740
The culprit should lead the way.

54
00:03:57,010 --> 00:03:59,480
- Let's go.
- No, wait...

55
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,550
Hurry up.

56
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:02,950
I was actually planning
to come see you.

57
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,720
About moving out that I brought up,

58
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,460
please just pretend
I never said anything.

59
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:15,230
Really? Can we really do that?

60
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:19,200
Yes. I think I was too rash.

61
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:21,300
Why even bring it up
in the first place?

62
00:04:21,530 --> 00:04:24,000
You made me lose 5,000 dollars
for nothing.

63
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,500
Pardon?

64
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:31,140
Well, the truth is, Teun Teun's mom,
we messed up.

65
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:34,280
To be exact, my mother did, not me.

66
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,780
Did you really have to
point fingers like that?

67
00:04:37,350 --> 00:04:39,150
What do you mean by that?

68
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,690
That 5,000 dollars you gave us
for moving expenses?

69
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:46,060
My mother went
and lost the whole thing.

70
00:04:46,590 --> 00:04:49,060
We should've just returned it to you
right then and there.

71
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:52,330
Wait, how could she have lost
that money?

72
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,670
Well...

73
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,140
Did you gamble it away
playing cards?

74
00:05:00,870 --> 00:05:01,870
Look, Teun Teun's mom,

75
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:04,210
we're not saying
we won't pay you back.

76
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:06,980
We'll definitely pay you back,

77
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:09,410
so could you please give us
a bit more time?

78
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:11,850
Even with time,
how do you expect to fix this?

79
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:16,490
Right now, we're taking on hourly
part-time gigs together as a team.

80
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:18,360
We're handing out flyers...

81
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:19,860
and waiting in lines
at popular restaurants.

82
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:21,690
Last week, didn't we catch...

83
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:23,630
- around 50 cockroaches?
- What?

84
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,430
Wait, are you saying...

85
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:28,870
you made her do
all those part-time jobs?

86
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:29,970
Yes!

87
00:05:30,670 --> 00:05:32,140
Teun Teun's mom,
I'm glad you brought that up.

88
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:35,440
That's no way to treat
an old woman like me.

89
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,240
You ungrateful brat.

90
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:42,810
Anyway, we'll be sure
to pay it back,

91
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,280
so please keep it a secret
from Eun Guk...

92
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,590
for now, okay?

93
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:55,590
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

94
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,700
Are you still mad?

95
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:02,500
I think you misunderstood me.

96
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:05,070
I didn't mean we should put your mom
in a nursing home for good.

97
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:08,570
I just thought it'd do her good
to get some fresh air and rest.

98
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:10,480
Is that really all you meant?

99
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,940
Of course.
Do you still not trust me?

100
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:16,110
Would I have chosen you
if I wasn't ready to care for her?

101
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:20,080
Also,

102
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:23,590
you can't just take for granted
that I'm willing to look after her.

103
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:26,220
Who lives with their in-laws
these days?

104
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,030
Even healthy ones live apart
like strangers.

105
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,870
That's why I asked you
to be more understanding.

106
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:35,170
Why do I always have to be
understanding?

107
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:36,970
She only ever asks for Ko Eun Seol.

108
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,870
How am I supposed
to understand that?

109
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:42,170
All right. I'll talk to my mom,

110
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:44,780
so please be more careful
from now on.

111
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:46,540
I have nothing to be careful about.

112
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:49,510
If she refuses to open up to me,

113
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,450
I'm just going to end up resentful.

114
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,650
And...

115
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,050
if this keeps up,

116
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:57,050
my dad won't just sit back
and watch.

117
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:00,020
You know how much he dotes on me.

118
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,660
Anyway, go tell your mother...

119
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:06,860
not to contact Ko Eun Seol
personally.

120
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,430
In fact, tell her
to block her completely.

121
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:20,980
Come in.

122
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,220
Here's the proposal
for the store event.

123
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,320
Thank you.

124
00:07:28,690 --> 00:07:31,390
Has Ms. Ko finished
the satisfaction survey...

125
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:32,460
she was preparing?

126
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,230
Well, you see...

127
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:36,960
Eun Seol left early yesterday.

128
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:40,700
- She left early?
- She seemed to have a severe fever.

129
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:42,900
We told her to go home early,

130
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:45,470
but she held out and collapsed
in the hallway.

131
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:04,160
Even after 30 years,

132
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,890
the scars haven't faded.

133
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:11,830
Still,

134
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,930
finding you, even late,

135
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:15,870
and being together like this...

136
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,600
makes up for all that lost time.

137
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,820
(Opening Ceremony)

138
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:37,490
(Cheongma Gallery Opening -
Cheongma Group Opens Art Space)

139
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,240
No...

140
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,080
No, this...

141
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,610
They're probably
just similar gloves.

142
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:06,380
They're just similar gloves...

143
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,400
Ko Eun Seol.

144
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:25,440
After seeing this,

145
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,570
she seems to have bought it
completely.

146
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:29,670
Unbelievable.

147
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:33,410
Who would've thought I'd ever
be grateful to An Guk Cheol?

148
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:41,020
Here's the list of people to greet
before the engagement.

149
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:43,690
Coordinate your schedule with Hae Ra
and go see them.

150
00:09:43,990 --> 00:09:46,060
Yes, sir. I'll do that.

151
00:09:46,190 --> 00:09:47,530
You might wonder...

152
00:09:47,530 --> 00:09:50,130
why you're making the rounds
just for an engagement,

153
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:53,430
but that's how things are done
here at Cheongma.

154
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:56,300
I visited our relatives
and greeted them...

155
00:09:56,370 --> 00:09:58,040
before my engagement as well.

156
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,900
Yes, I understand.

157
00:10:00,270 --> 00:10:02,010
You're only getting engaged,

158
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:04,540
but it's no different from marriage.

159
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,310
And as for the wedding,

160
00:10:07,610 --> 00:10:10,150
the second half of next year
seems appropriate.

161
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:11,520
What do you think, Chief Cha?

162
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:13,220
Next year?

163
00:10:13,650 --> 00:10:16,450
Well, Hae Ra seemed fine with it.

164
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:20,060
That works for me as well.

165
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:22,990
Becoming a member
of Cheongma means...

166
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:26,530
stepping foot into
an entirely different world.

167
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:30,500
Of course, heavy responsibility
comes with it.

168
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,470
However,

169
00:10:32,570 --> 00:10:35,310
the power and authority
you'll possess...

170
00:10:35,370 --> 00:10:36,870
will be immense.

171
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:43,450
In any case, welcome to Cheongma.
My sincere congratulations.

172
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,050
Thank you.

173
00:10:46,950 --> 00:10:50,960
I'll do my very best
not to disappoint you, sir.

174
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:02,030
(CEO's Office)

175
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,680
Keeping Chief Cha close...

176
00:11:14,510 --> 00:11:16,880
should quell this anxiety.

177
00:11:18,450 --> 00:11:21,020
I'll have to tame him completely.

178
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:25,390
Are you home, Mr. Seok Jin?

179
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:27,490
Did you have a fun day at daycare?

180
00:11:27,890 --> 00:11:32,360
Yes, I finished making
all the bookmarks there.

181
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:33,800
Good.

182
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,400
- Am I getting a few?
- Of course.

183
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:38,470
You'll get a lot, Mr. Seok Jin.

184
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,340
All right. I'll go change first.

185
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:43,070
Mr. Seok Jin, wait.

186
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:44,980
Yes?

187
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:47,580
I want to give
one of the bookmarks...

188
00:11:47,650 --> 00:11:49,980
to the nice lady, too.

189
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:52,380
Can I go see her?

190
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:53,480
Well...

191
00:11:54,590 --> 00:11:57,120
I heard she's very sick right now.

192
00:11:57,590 --> 00:11:59,960
So maybe give it to her
next time, okay?

193
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,760
What could be wrong with her?

194
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,160
The nice lady...

195
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:09,170
Just how sick is she?

196
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:30,190
Mom, did you see the lighter
that was here?

197
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:35,430
I don't know where it is.
Besides, I don't like that lighter.

198
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,900
I'm certain I left it right here.

199
00:12:38,330 --> 00:12:40,930
It seemed like Dad's,
so I kept it safe.

200
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,670
Did Auntie from daycare take it?

201
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:46,870
She hasn't been in your room,
Mr. Seok Jin.

202
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:50,170
Wait. Last time,

203
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:54,310
Director Joo came in
to check your clothes.

204
00:12:55,850 --> 00:12:57,010
Director Joo?

205
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:01,150
Yes, to check your clothing size.

206
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,230
Was it Director Joo?

207
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:16,200
Nice lady, please don't be sick.

208
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:18,870
Eat this and get your strength back.

209
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:22,840
I'm going to make you
some delicious beef porridge.

210
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,590
(Cheongma
Customer Appreciation Event)

211
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:39,720
(Chief Cha Seok Jin, Cheongma Group)

212
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:46,200
(Customer Appreciation Event)

213
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,530
(Shoe fitting consultation
and customer satisfaction survey)

214
00:13:52,570 --> 00:13:53,640
Here's my card.

215
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:56,070
(Cha Seok Jin)

216
00:13:58,310 --> 00:13:59,980
Right.

217
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,550
This is where I should go.

218
00:14:05,050 --> 00:14:06,880
That's An Guk Cheol for you.

219
00:14:08,990 --> 00:14:10,520
Luck is on my side.

220
00:14:11,190 --> 00:14:12,690
Luck is definitely on my side.

221
00:14:13,590 --> 00:14:15,860
It looks like Ko Eun Seol
can't make it today,

222
00:14:15,930 --> 00:14:17,160
so let's start without her.

223
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:24,240
You actually came to work.

224
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,840
I thought
you were taking the day off.

225
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,110
You're welcome to take off forever.

226
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:32,580
Eun Seol, how are you feeling?

227
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:34,210
I'm fine.

228
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:38,520
Thank you for taking care of me,
including the hospital matter.

229
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,420
Director Joo, why are you
looking after Ko Eun Seol?

230
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,150
The circumstances called for it.

231
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:49,430
Eun Seol, have some of this.
It's organic chamomile.

232
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:58,140
You must still be recovering,
so drink this...

233
00:14:58,540 --> 00:14:59,970
regularly.

234
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,520
Let's form the panel of judges
with prominent outside figures.

235
00:15:14,750 --> 00:15:16,520
That way,
the press will cover it first,

236
00:15:16,590 --> 00:15:18,120
and it'll be good
for the foundation's image.

237
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:22,530
I think we need people
with on-site experience.

238
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:25,130
People like vocational instructors
or social workers...

239
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,630
from correctional facilities.

240
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:31,040
That's a great idea, Eun Seol.
Let's proceed in that direction.

241
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,370
Secretary Choi,
compile a list of candidates...

242
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,940
based on Eun Seol's suggestions...

243
00:15:37,010 --> 00:15:38,580
so we can move forward
at the next meeting.

244
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:40,980
- Director Joo.
- Good work, everyone.

245
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:49,420
Director.

246
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,220
Is Ko Eun Seol
holding something over you?

247
00:15:52,590 --> 00:15:54,160
Don't be ridiculous.

248
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:56,560
You have to handle her gently
to keep her in line.

249
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:43,340
Ms. Park?

250
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,780
Oh, no...

251
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:57,520
Ms. Park, what are you doing here?
What about daycare?

252
00:16:58,190 --> 00:17:01,960
It's not what you think. I just...

253
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,990
Did you come to give this
to Seok Jin?

254
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:05,660
- What is it?
- What?

255
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:07,770
Nothing. It's nothing.

256
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:09,630
I asked what it is.

257
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:11,800
It's porridge.

258
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:15,140
I heard the nice lady was sick,

259
00:17:15,210 --> 00:17:17,840
so I made beef porridge for her.

260
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:20,080
This isn't for you, Hae Ra.

261
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,480
What, the nice lady?

262
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,050
- Ko Eun Seol?
- Yes.

263
00:17:27,950 --> 00:17:29,720
Wait, what are you doing?

264
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,490
Hae Ra, that's not it.

265
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:39,430
So...

266
00:17:40,330 --> 00:17:41,930
Ko Eun Seol is sick,

267
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,870
and you made this for her?

268
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:49,270
I'm just going to drop this off
and leave.

269
00:17:49,370 --> 00:17:50,770
I'll be quick.

270
00:17:57,550 --> 00:18:00,050
Ms. Park, why do you only ask
for Ko Eun Seol?

271
00:18:00,850 --> 00:18:04,460
It's always Ko Eun Seol with you.

272
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:10,860
Who does she think she is?

273
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:14,800
Ms. Park.

274
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:17,230
Do I look like a joke to you?

275
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,170
Because of you,
Seok Jin and I keep drifting apart.

276
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:25,080
This is all your fault!

277
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,520
If you keep doing this,

278
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:38,220
Seok Jin won't be happy.

279
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:42,760
Because I'll make sure
he's never happy.

280
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:47,730
I'm more than capable of that.

281
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:49,770
You know I am.

282
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,070
Boss.

283
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:24,700
You seem to have
a lot more energy today.

284
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,700
Do I?

285
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:29,610
Yes, you're usually struggling
around this time of day.

286
00:19:29,910 --> 00:19:31,740
Taking care of Teun Teun,
housework...

287
00:19:32,410 --> 00:19:34,440
You're usually exhausted
by the afternoon.

288
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:39,880
As of yesterday, I hired someone
to help with the housework.

289
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,650
A housekeeper?

290
00:19:42,350 --> 00:19:43,350
Yes.

291
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:47,090
If things were that hard,
you should've let me know.

292
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:49,560
I'd run over anytime
and help you out.

293
00:19:49,830 --> 00:19:51,030
That's all right.

294
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:54,500
She agreed to take care
of the housework for now.

295
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,770
What kind of person is she?

296
00:19:57,630 --> 00:19:58,940
It's not a guy, right?

297
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,040
No, it's not.

298
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:03,570
What's her personality like?

299
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:05,740
Well, she's a bit...

300
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:10,110
cranky, and she seems
to have quite a temper.

301
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,380
Either way, she's a bit unusual.

302
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:14,280
Then let her go immediately.

303
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:17,290
What if she ends up
doing something to hurt you?

304
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:20,120
Don't worry. I can handle her.

305
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,670
If you keep doing this,

306
00:20:35,710 --> 00:20:37,240
Seok Jin won't be happy.

307
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:41,950
Because I'll make sure
he's never happy.

308
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:45,820
I'm more than capable of that.

309
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,860
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

310
00:21:01,870 --> 00:21:02,870
Yes, Auntie.

311
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:06,140
Seok Jin, are you busy right now?

312
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,740
I was just about to head home.

313
00:21:09,410 --> 00:21:12,910
When you get home,
make sure your mom eats something.

314
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:16,010
She hasn't left her room
for a while now.

315
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:18,420
Sure, I'll get her to eat something.

316
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:24,690
I'm home.

317
00:21:25,190 --> 00:21:27,990
Oh, you're back.

318
00:21:28,690 --> 00:21:29,690
Yes.

319
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:32,730
Wait, Eun Seol.

320
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,770
Come sit here for a second.

321
00:21:41,170 --> 00:21:43,010
Is there something
you wanted to say?

322
00:21:43,070 --> 00:21:45,280
Yes, but it's nothing big.

323
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:49,710
Does the company offer
any employee loans?

324
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:52,250
- A loan?
- That's right.

325
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:54,380
I'm sure your company offers them.

326
00:21:54,380 --> 00:21:57,520
We can only turn
to third-party lenders, you see.

327
00:21:58,820 --> 00:22:00,660
Why do you need a loan
all of a sudden?

328
00:22:01,090 --> 00:22:02,390
Are you short on cash?

329
00:22:02,390 --> 00:22:04,700
Aren't we always?

330
00:22:05,330 --> 00:22:08,470
I have to cover
an unexpected expense,

331
00:22:08,470 --> 00:22:09,970
so can we...

332
00:22:10,530 --> 00:22:12,900
take out a loan in your name?

333
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:14,540
Mom!

334
00:22:16,610 --> 00:22:18,510
No, Eun Seol, don't worry about it.

335
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,640
Grandma's just talking nonsense.

336
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,710
You don't need to get a loan.

337
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:42,970
I don't know
what words Hee Jung left behind,

338
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:46,000
but the family who raised you...

339
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,370
came looking for me.

340
00:22:49,810 --> 00:22:52,740
They demanded money for raising you.

341
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:56,680
I was just so terrified.

342
00:23:02,150 --> 00:23:03,150
Money...

343
00:23:04,790 --> 00:23:05,960
They asked for money?

344
00:23:18,870 --> 00:23:22,470
So, did you talk to CEO Park?

345
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:23,610
Yes.

346
00:23:23,770 --> 00:23:26,340
I told him to watch himself.

347
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,810
Can you believe CEO Park...

348
00:23:29,350 --> 00:23:31,310
is having an affair
with a younger woman?

349
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:34,180
To give him an alibi,

350
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:37,820
Young Hoon lied and told me
they were going golfing together.

351
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:41,360
I see.

352
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:46,060
Men and their loyalty,
I really don't get it sometimes.

353
00:23:48,670 --> 00:23:49,730
Still,

354
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:52,370
that alibi...

355
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:58,410
is a great way for both sides
to cover for each other, isn't it?

356
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:02,480
I mean, really.

357
00:24:02,580 --> 00:24:06,250
If you ever find yourself
in a situation like CEO Park's,

358
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:10,320
it'd be a pretty good deal
for covering each other.

359
00:24:12,490 --> 00:24:16,230
Well, I suppose so.

360
00:24:16,430 --> 00:24:18,130
Except that's not me.

361
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:20,830
I'm not having an affair
like CEO Park.

362
00:24:21,430 --> 00:24:22,570
If it were a deal,

363
00:24:22,570 --> 00:24:24,900
I'd definitely be getting
the bad end of it.

364
00:24:24,970 --> 00:24:26,300
Right?

365
00:24:26,870 --> 00:24:30,040
Because you would never do
such a thing.

366
00:24:51,430 --> 00:24:52,800
Let's talk for a moment.

367
00:24:57,030 --> 00:24:58,700
He's calling for me again?

368
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:26,200
I assume you cleared your schedule?

369
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:27,960
Yes.

370
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:30,600
I made arrangements in Yangpyeong
for this weekend.

371
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:34,640
All right, good.
You won't stand me up again?

372
00:25:36,310 --> 00:25:38,510
I won't make the same mistake twice.

373
00:25:40,410 --> 00:25:44,010
Director Joo,
ever since I joined Cheongma,

374
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:46,580
I've felt like an empty shell.

375
00:25:47,820 --> 00:25:49,090
But things have changed lately.

376
00:25:50,390 --> 00:25:51,820
Thanks to you, Director Joo,

377
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:53,890
I feel human again.

378
00:25:58,190 --> 00:25:59,200
Me too.

379
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:04,230
Because of you,
I feel whole at last.

380
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:21,990
I'm having trouble walking.

381
00:26:22,050 --> 00:26:23,890
Could I see some comfortable shoes?

382
00:26:23,950 --> 00:26:26,820
I'll recommend some shoes
that'll be easy on your feet.

383
00:26:26,890 --> 00:26:27,990
Please have a seat here.

384
00:26:28,790 --> 00:26:29,790
Thank you.

385
00:26:46,510 --> 00:26:47,840
Why don't you try walking in them?

386
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:54,680
That feels so much better.

387
00:26:55,190 --> 00:26:56,750
They're light, too.

388
00:26:57,350 --> 00:27:00,090
You're so pretty and very kind.

389
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:02,560
I'll take these.

390
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:04,360
Sure, let me help you with that.

391
00:27:12,240 --> 00:27:13,700
Ji Ho, Yong Hwa.

392
00:27:23,050 --> 00:27:26,780
Excuse me, could you recommend
some good shoes for me?

393
00:27:40,230 --> 00:27:41,230
Please have a seat right here.

394
00:27:55,910 --> 00:27:59,650
Do you work here?
You are mighty kind.

395
00:28:09,690 --> 00:28:12,060
Try sliding your foot in here.

396
00:28:12,330 --> 00:28:15,430
My foot isn't going in easily.

397
00:28:15,470 --> 00:28:16,870
Do you have a bigger size?

398
00:28:20,370 --> 00:28:21,370
Just a moment.

399
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:38,960
What the heck? Where did he go?

400
00:28:46,300 --> 00:28:47,900
Who took the coffee that was here?

401
00:29:01,910 --> 00:29:02,910
With just this,

402
00:29:04,150 --> 00:29:05,780
Joo Ae Sook's life will totally...

403
00:29:06,750 --> 00:29:07,980
be done for.

404
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:11,620
Just you wait, Ae Sook.

405
00:29:11,720 --> 00:29:12,920
Soon enough,

406
00:29:14,660 --> 00:29:16,530
I'll come see you with my daughter.

407
00:29:30,910 --> 00:29:32,940
You worked so hard today.

408
00:29:34,740 --> 00:29:36,380
I'm not just saying this
because you're my daughter,

409
00:29:37,450 --> 00:29:40,320
but how did you get to be
so kind-hearted?

410
00:29:40,850 --> 00:29:42,090
You're so friendly, too.

411
00:29:42,690 --> 00:29:45,790
Not at all. I was just doing my job.

412
00:29:47,090 --> 00:29:50,090
Eun Seol, I'm sure you'll end up
with someone great.

413
00:29:50,990 --> 00:29:53,360
They say good people
recognize each other.

414
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:56,030
Evil people do too, of course.

415
00:29:58,270 --> 00:29:59,270
Right.

416
00:30:00,570 --> 00:30:01,570
Eun Seol,

417
00:30:03,340 --> 00:30:05,070
I've been thinking.

418
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,240
How about you move out...

419
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:09,910
of your current place?

420
00:30:11,080 --> 00:30:12,080
What?

421
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:14,350
If it's okay with you,

422
00:30:15,220 --> 00:30:17,950
I'd like to get you
a studio apartment.

423
00:30:19,220 --> 00:30:22,190
It'd also be wonderful
to study design professionally.

424
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:29,230
This is the design school
Hae Ra attended.

425
00:30:30,570 --> 00:30:32,740
If you study hard there
for four years,

426
00:30:32,900 --> 00:30:34,470
it's bound to help.

427
00:30:36,110 --> 00:30:37,110
Here.

428
00:30:37,510 --> 00:30:38,580
And...

429
00:30:39,140 --> 00:30:40,180
as for the retrial,

430
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:42,350
I've been preparing for it.

431
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:49,350
Now that Team Leader Seo
ended up like that,

432
00:30:49,990 --> 00:30:51,790
you're going to need
a new lawyer anyway.

433
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:56,460
What do you say about handing it
to the lawyer I found?

434
00:31:00,460 --> 00:31:02,470
Yes, sounds good.

435
00:31:04,170 --> 00:31:05,170
All right,

436
00:31:05,900 --> 00:31:08,470
let's give it everything we've got.

437
00:31:09,010 --> 00:31:10,840
I'll do my best to help you.

438
00:31:21,420 --> 00:31:22,420
That's right.

439
00:31:24,020 --> 00:31:26,160
I'm allowed to dream too,
at least once.

440
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:34,430
That's okay, right, Mom?

441
00:31:38,270 --> 00:31:42,010
The annual tuition
is about 80,000 to 90,000 dollars.

442
00:31:42,410 --> 00:31:44,440
And for a place
in a safe neighborhood,

443
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:48,540
the rent would be
around 40,000 dollars a year.

444
00:31:50,610 --> 00:31:52,350
I don't care about safety,

445
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:55,120
so just look for the cheapest area.

446
00:31:55,690 --> 00:31:57,390
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

447
00:31:57,390 --> 00:31:59,060
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

448
00:32:00,690 --> 00:32:02,890
Darn, it's so freaking expensive.

449
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:06,060
Why do I have to spend
that kind of money on Ko Eun Seol?

450
00:32:09,170 --> 00:32:11,800
I'll coax her
with studying abroad...

451
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:14,500
and send her
as far away as possible.

452
00:32:25,280 --> 00:32:28,350
It's always Ko Eun Seol with you.

453
00:32:30,190 --> 00:32:31,190
Kang Young Hoon.

454
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:33,520
You need to stop.

455
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:35,290
You're going to get
into serious trouble.

456
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:37,160
Let go of me.

457
00:32:37,630 --> 00:32:39,300
Just keep your mouth shut
and everything will be fine.

458
00:32:57,980 --> 00:32:58,980
Where did she go?

459
00:33:02,190 --> 00:33:03,220
Seok Jin!

460
00:33:28,850 --> 00:33:30,480
Just wait a moment.

461
00:33:30,710 --> 00:33:32,180
I'll have breakfast ready
in no time.

462
00:33:33,280 --> 00:33:34,350
Mom?

463
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:37,590
I made doenjang stew, your favorite.

464
00:33:38,190 --> 00:33:40,660
Take off your jacket first
so the smell doesn't stick to it.

465
00:34:07,780 --> 00:34:11,490
(A Trap Called Desire)

466
00:34:11,690 --> 00:34:14,720
Are you saying you're going here?
Someone like you?

467
00:34:14,790 --> 00:34:16,830
Did you land yourself
a wealthy sponsor?

468
00:34:16,930 --> 00:34:20,230
Did you really have to demand money
just for raising me?

469
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:22,700
Was getting that money
really necessary?

470
00:34:22,770 --> 00:34:23,800
Ms. Park's going to see a doctor.

471
00:34:23,870 --> 00:34:25,170
To check something, apparently.

472
00:34:25,300 --> 00:34:27,170
Mom...

473
00:34:27,170 --> 00:34:29,040
When they leave for their honeymoon,

474
00:34:29,110 --> 00:34:31,270
that's when I should strike.

475
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:32,780
Yes!

476
00:34:33,110 --> 00:34:35,240
Wait for me, my daughter.

477
00:34:35,280 --> 00:34:37,950
Come on,
it's my daughter's engagement party.

478
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:40,250
A father can't miss that.

479
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:43,090
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
